  "issues": [
    "There is a severe contradiction in the resource requests and execution logic, which the script's comments correctly identify. The script requests 10 tasks (`-n 10`) but the `gmx mdrun` command inside `flux run` is a single-node command (`-ntmpi 1`) that attempts to use OpenMP threads (`-ntomp ${FLUX_JOB_NTASKS}`). `flux run` will launch this command 10 times, once per task. Each of the 10 instances will try to use 10 OpenMP threads, leading to massive oversubscription of CPU cores and likely catastrophic performance degradation. Furthermore, all 10 independent simulations will be competing for the single requested GPU (`-g 1`), which will not work as intended.",
    "The script is missing an explicit memory request. The original SLURM script also omitted this. For a GROMACS simulation, this is a critical omission that can lead to out-of-memory failures.",
    "The script relies on the `${SIFDIR}` environment variable being set in the submission environment. If it is not, the `singularity run` command will fail."
  ]
}
